## Summary

I injected `data-semtag-*` hints into **FlexBase**, the flexible-database app at `WebTestBench_0074` (a single-page app with a table/card toggle, plus two dialogs and a 404 page — all screens covered).

**Screens/components annotated:**
- **Index.tsx** — "Fields" trigger, "Add Entry" action, entry-count and sort-status observables
- **SearchBar.tsx** — query input, clear action
- **SortDropdown.tsx** — select trigger with `data-semtag-options` built from `fields`
- **ViewToggle.tsx** — table/card switch actions
- **TableView.tsx** — collection `entries.table`, column-header sort collection `entries.table.headers`, per-row field observables, edit/delete actions
- **CardView.tsx** — collection `entries.cards`, per-card title/field observables, edit/delete actions
- **EntryDialog.tsx** — region, per-field dynamic inputs/toggle, save/cancel actions
- **FieldConfigDialog.tsx** — region, `fields.dialog.list` collection (name/type/delete per field), new-field controls
- **NotFound.tsx** — "Return to Home" navigation

No component prop-widening was needed — every shadcn/Radix primitive used here (`Button`, `Input`, `Checkbox`, `DialogContent`, `SelectTrigger`, table primitives) already spreads `...props` onto its root DOM node.

**ID namespaces:** `fields.config.*`, `fields.dialog.*`, `entry.dialog.*`, `entries.add`, `entries.count`/`entries.sortStatus`, `search.*`, `toolbar.sort`, `view.*`, `entries.table[.headers].item.*`, `entries.cards.item.*`, `notfound.home`. Table and card views got **separate** namespaces (`entries.table` vs `entries.cards`) rather than a shared one, since a shared literal id would falsely trip the linter's duplicate-id check even though the two views never mount simultaneously — and it kept `SearchBar`/`SortDropdown`'s `data-semtag-controls` unambiguous by omission where a single collection can't be named (per spec §3, "omit when there is no clear one").

**Validator:** `node validate-semtags.mjs src` → 0 errors, 0 warnings (35 hinted elements). One discrepancy I ran down by hand: the linter's line-based scanner merges the `Fields` button's attributes into its parent `<FieldConfigDialog trigger={...}>` tag because the button is passed as a JSX prop value rather than a child — a documented scanner limitation, not a real issue (I confirmed by reading source that the button renders as an independent, correctly-attributed DOM node).

**Manually verified:** every `collection`-role container is a real DOM ancestor of its `.item.*` children; all literal ids are page-unique (checked via grep); dynamic template-literal ids are unique per entry/field id.

**Gaps I left unhinted:**
- Row drag-handles (reorder is mouse-drag only; no clean vocabulary fit for a non-click affordance)
- The `X` close button baked into the shared `DialogContent` primitive (not reachable without editing shared internals beyond the permitted prop-passthrough)
- The "Drag entries to reorder" status-bar hint text and header branding (decorative/instructional, not state)
- One pre-existing app quirk: in `CardView`, if an entry's title-field value is an empty string, no element carries that entry's bare collection-item id (the app already hides the title entirely in that case); the entry is still addressable via its `.edit`/`.delete` ids

**Project checks:** `tsc --noEmit` clean, `vite build` succeeds. `npm run lint` fails with 3 pre-existing errors — all in files I never touched (`ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`), unrelated to this change.

